{"type":"message","id":"f1d8fb12","parentId":"962a029d","timestamp":"2026-04-09T19:41:30.686Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Addressing tool malfunction**\n\nIt seems like I’m experiencing a weird tool malfunction. My best option is to use the write function to overwrite the entire file. This should help resolve the issue. I’m focused on making sure everything gets documented correctly and not leaving anything incomplete. I want to double-check that I’m doing this properly to ensure things stay organized and functional. Let’s move forward with this approach!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_05ae207fdae919ce0169d800cc37d8819183fd9eaa30561029\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2ADNa9-IOPkii7tp3V2fvbDNm3Mcx6qP8wYPuZO53Qlis9oPYsRCKDKrP71k2z0Wzg9QW0VWd4qQwKDSQyBtZmP1oNf9H3SxpB7777MVcwo7pNYElq5H0XkmRhVltDviTB0IcePTReK2WVw9sY25plKVVm_kkfC3UQA_5dGAIA04_hbRo8MsymaFcvl_M1gzwTNdq0RfIYpV1KlUxYnPnh-OCOQAmgMJXNkJomu1f7KwrJU4Je6woLWrPCQGCbl7yS2rn20cE88EJtwoeCojMyh7XHG9mMLIE49e1O4rJATXQotrM9-GtjQneSjIZxB0r3HfeCUfOAPlj3opBwNBlghwXxkD2SOvq2yi8sZw2bVg_5L64JwWbZUuk-wCqACSxXwDOa4mFr18JjgEN9knWr08z-sY6cYS_HhBQPyGs3OJC6HiTO3-7QWP6aRWOUt2TiCc-unHgUk_wjJd9i6meN60GlcpmN0BXg2wImkMozMZ0OaJJUkU8lDAzQRlT2tFD8c9YasdfcA718zfo7jjyrP4356uErHAIMYbcxZTY1TOuKiwtscAIXWO6h7_7G3jP8gxvfoJZQSF86LG9_yMVMrQY06EizQY8OJYqRqjuar3Qg_MXBpY-KXaf1fVBcdsI6KIV2-Z4ynsB48N7XQJrDJrY-z_qL-ysdYFi2U1VYc-K5d941_w6I2OVifKn26mJaXejSSBxWzBMbIGyzRNPwTDCNj0GV5HdVdJi_VyK78tPB5MKCutFf7JKYH3Vo3a2GAWRPozQwmnUhgTDLYKSmQBcebLudxkdGLfsRpHWCvI0qlqrSZl_YCfzR1Dl4FuSSQLzW-_fyEwjcy7muzG7zgxPfD9QZFwjKlt_Kdfdxld1ssT12oC70njB7FZNxiDv7GGvGkYV-UCaL-xwA-esj9bgQ==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Addressing tool malfunction**\\n\\nIt seems like I’m experiencing a weird tool malfunction. My best option is to use the write function to overwrite the entire file. This should help resolve the issue. I’m focused on making sure everything gets documented correctly and not leaving anything incomplete. I want to double-check that I’m doing this properly to ensure things stay organized and functional. Let’s move forward with this approach!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/scripts/query_slm_expert_backup.py\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nimport argparse\\nimport json\\nimport sys\\nfrom urllib import error, request\\n\\nQUERY_ENDPOINT = \\\"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/chat\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\\n    try:\\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n        return body.strip()\\n\\n    if isinstance(parsed, str):\\n        return parsed.strip()\\n\\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\\n\\n    for key in (\\\"answer\\\", \\\"Answer\\\", \\\"response\\\", \\\"message\\\"):\\n        value = parsed.get(key)\\n        if value is not None:\\n            if isinstance(value, str):\\n                text = value.strip()\\n                try:\\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict):\\n                        for nested_key in (\\\"answer\\\", \\\"Answer\\\", \\\"response\\\", \\\"message\\\"):\\n                            nested_value = nested.get(nested_key)\\n                            if nested_value is not None:\\n                                return str(nested_value).strip()\\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n                    pass\\n                return text\\n            return json.dumps(value, indent=2)\\n\\n    data = parsed.get(\\\"data\\\")\\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\\n        for key in (\\\"answer\\\", \\\"Answer\\\", \\\"response\\\", \\\"message\\\"):\\n            value = data.get(key)\\n            if value is not None:\\n                return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\\n\\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\\n\\n\\ndef post_json(url: str, payload: dict, timeout: int) -> str:\\n    req = request.Request(\\n        url,\\n        data=json.dumps(payload).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n        headers={\\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\", \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json\\\"},\\n        method=\\\"POST\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    try:\\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\\n            return resp.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\\n        detail = e.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"HTTP {e.code} from {url}: {detail}\\\") from e\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Request to {url} failed: {e}\\\") from e\\n\\n\\ndef call_endpoint(question: str, timeout: int = 45) -> str:\\n    body = post_json(QUERY_ENDPOINT, {\\\"question\\\": question}, timeout)\\n    return extract_answer(body)\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\\n        description=\\\"Query the backup SLM chat endpoint with a single question payload\\\"\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--question\\\", required=True, help=\\\"Question to send to the chat endpoint\\\")\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--timeout\\\", type=int, default=45)\\n    args = parser.parse_args()\\n\\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.question, timeout=args.timeout)\\n    print(answer)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    try:\\n        main()\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        print(f\\\"ERROR: {exc}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        sys.exit(1)\\n\"}","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05ae207fdae919ce0169d800cdec6c819192d1039b90db1f43\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_05ae207fdae919ce0169d800daa12c81919eb35c3bef05eee6\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2ADbhe_MAK6fR0FP0daMU71CfE4M56Fpvot-peurj4PijvXOvn7vvwOh_AdiJOYF9453zNmwgCSNQBH52h1wEdKuLRuJvHAzsQ3EbPEQdeybYj2UOWuGFikS53nt-KDXhRTzu0oNai6dh4ju_6BPl4V_3_S6dbmSd6lpKALyCkNYy8LTw6LoBZV3dc9JzzrB_ByiAHhJ2kRuljwKmoZM88MZd2j9tml3fSnzgVF9UMpSMqki20rDjYHJSs8vFoJnJ8GaXWGyJ4slZAMm4zux8oSpio36MhvdZAXB9VadZks6EKfmw4XbN61njJyDI6HwXawtClJLGdN-xqARt-_XuTs550Ent81DdBJUA2sdkQa6Yd-5AgSZKC6PjXYICvVUWTUJOKpQtM4TP3MJjG7gpXwsBBrGGzNEYSxrUhFcDwhxpoTPNXtx625pLFFF5Jb_ey6BLEppf0VBCSceb3ViCPnLXF4YQfjpnMT7q4geqjUbEpVma8xliwG9cvOc5sfPIrgrK_a2ZgbHSCRLGaXpNqFcPyBRoJJHiB1-Ug_fyEr5ElAREk7RawYneQEY7WLNtRHMvh_blXk5D1dTmtX7BpYTgP28z92vBVwATfQUTRV3I7HmAbg5UBwVkOd9wNRFUY8U1kthCYiYVfGKA0bLzJKlfstYS_nvFs7TFGHQawIJoaFF5JpK9wpy76wpr-c4IdNtKkKxbX16pOF6Vl0Q0Cvni3CHWfmp6Qt3q7tbt0nSULAytIuoZxHXTdbv1Z7f29PCykoedb8IflJAvoXMNceEGzOTuQVdMOD8fOLzahF_1guSCPKoERqj1xXECeM0tsa907oNoCN71edpbxqPRk4OZ5v_NOXLrV4vfBnXWSA8RW8=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: slm-expert-backup\\ndescription: Query the backup SLM chat endpoint by sending only a single `question` field to `/chat`, then process the returned answer in the calling agent. Use when this backup skill should ignore domain routing and any extra request fields and must send a minimal payload shaped like `{ \\\"question\\\": \\\"...\\\" }`.\\n---\\n\\n# SLM Expert Backup\\n\\nUse this skill to query the backup SLM through the `/chat` endpoint with a minimal JSON payload.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Build one question string.\\n   - Send only the question text.\\n   - Do not include domains, patient context objects, routing hints, or other request fields.\\n\\n2. Query the backup endpoint.\\n   - Run:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/query_slm_expert_backup.py \\\\\\n  --question \\\"Which are the latest user symptoms?\\\"\\n```\\n\\n   - The script sends this payload shape:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"Which are the latest user symptoms?\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n   - Endpoint:\\n\\n```text\\nhttp://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/chat\\n```\\n\\n3. Read the response.\\n   - Prefer a clean text answer.\\n   - Accept common shapes such as `answer`, `Answer`, `response`, `message`, or raw text.\\n   - If the endpoint returns nested JSON encoded as a string, extract the useful answer text when possible.\\n   - If parsing is ambiguous, keep the best raw text and say so briefly in your own reasoning.\\n   - If the answer is `Not found in context.`, report that plainly instead of inventing content.\\n\\n4. Process the answer in the calling agent.\\n   - Do not treat the endpoint output as the final user-facing answer by default.\\n   - Use it as an input to the agent’s own reasoning or synthesis.\\n   - Preserve uncertainty and avoid overstating confidence.\\n\\n## Output pattern\\n\\nReturn a response that includes:\\n\\n- **SLM finding**: the key content from the model answer, cleaned up if needed\\n- **Agent interpretation**: the calling agent’s processed interpretation grounded in the available context\\n- **Cautions / next steps**: only when relevant\\n\"}","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05ae207fdae919ce0169d800db43ac819199fd4431a80fd79a\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Updating prompt-templates**\n\nI think the prompt-template might be outdated, which could lead to some stale references. It's probably a good idea to update it to ensure that everything is current and relevant. I want to avoid any confusion or misunderstandings that could arise from using old information. Maybe I'll look into the latest guidelines or best practices to incorporate into the template! It'll definitely help in keeping things fresh and engaging.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_05ae207fdae919ce0169d800e458d88191b40b3f67fa99bc32\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2ADlI9xyJiSkOvrFgXJ_Jc1ejm5qEO9Ftq2EIN0srZOgVq-Lg_pSgmPIMMsWchP2_ynt1c8MRS72EA7X2b0gydGSUl9YKuzZ8fnI68Nhc_wwIzSlMbs9UykfsolMlAppprH5OV3vlJvfvkAz59obk6SUSTZFbDWvAPHf7Htdy6TENXn45j1NlMChPmDg9xYyRRQEAOpGnlyb-YbzLDwWT8ZG0G_qNC15QafmL2wWrK0sAuoNdsfb0AqSNa31g-3SxF88qT1iknVrFLTWUpuc3HYNucnLNuKDBkxFpahuHtilckL6zn-2kqc4ffsFJTgDUKAFMCZmx0p23ytFZFSvQKay1kkEwH13_aH1And6vGvTC5eZ0Yt9SzvZmLvlPMVfdptG4weTf9nHAAQYTlqNQbyNP571MJPOexLtDZP-_CNq2rAMph3-824Fj6jj3McuzdEb52jqB9v5clEY6twEChPk2Bf5LUkw9i0Xy7wwYPD0ag_G4DNijPoOrpYKGhBseytKkJrp2P_Eraprw0I7oFXPWxroxFy6fx5QwJzeJnNOv0xeUdJ8d4MBX2wNajWbLMvMBxOBk1oImLVVfJmpYm_uH_g6Rpq5pUu9WqSYQAkfVksU4a8bQcG8JgaLCjON03LcWGzl6XzM2e_-VPg44Rhmv9bux5Wh_9s8N5EWUx0SFxQDW2_ZtMQHYWQLjZtagzFlXkqDDPluV1fHsX-HTWfd6enZoCg7bj1_y977kOmHh7mbPPAfH6myfGbXQyrYLfnl8Alf2XCciFXLJIpZM39KQkdx3yOUwOD2LfE4kQjOYH_GFgGGnq2btJ9fdFCs5rgbemoQAS26M42VnaQpWcHNC9LGY_RRN-N502KiRQRq3-83mO2t_AYJbcWbSr_TkV3TdDHvJH0dGcFEehe_xa2iMdqnUnIT0a-Pwx1uYpf9ctc=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Updating prompt-templates**\\n\\nI think the prompt-template might be outdated, which could lead to some stale references. It's probably a good idea to update it to ensure that everything is current and relevant. I want to avoid any confusion or misunderstandings that could arise from using old information. Maybe I'll look into the latest guidelines or best practices to incorporate into the template! It'll definitely help in keeping things fresh and engaging.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/references/prompt-template.md\",\"content\":\"# Backup SLM question template\\n\\nUse this shape when preparing a question for the backup `/chat` endpoint.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"Which are the latest user symptoms?\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\nGuidance:\\n- Send only the `question` field.\\n- Do not send `domains` or any other extra request fields.\\n- Keep the question concise.\\n- The calling agent should interpret the returned answer instead of relaying it blindly.\\n\"}","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05ae207fdae919ce0169d800e5fdc081918d5482fce7a714f4\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_05ae207fdae919ce0169d800e737e08191ba6654a215ad3bcb\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2ADps6xfs8gTJhaL5bMcZBw9OVQ31Qjrykv13csNMQFNgtj7lJSTVBJNlKe9tGSXcjp7KIm9SR_CAE339gB2xKiAJOrusVOetswe7TKe15mX7WNLGQHGPMMtiDJ8AaCQbrXWgC06f8HON3YyzR9MOYXJuApJ2EXh0ePfFBqHkWoLQw1in0pGJoVI57NiJ8cvgob6i6-6-nfNUG0MLLAwe5kZfYXR3StbCJ76FvU5LjC7rfPQMYnnSciFC3stA_0MBkyEAoHdGr7PyAsuIkWomVEVJslbP_9boulFgWvH6astDBDPLKkM861EnYdVtOM5f5W_Tykis2IufU0a-8IyBLDuRxtFcpqpIOl6snh8q7oEdBgBTOXsd-OXy1xNduMpDTSpyAZOBqMBYS55OF1HYBDMm_zm0YL53CIN_7iq1lGiKAE300mmkQdaoyco6_zt99yrEXmSWuJvUiDga52uZgzz8zrUw6-fSzs1jSd8zwnB7hRXKx9MWxVeOPOkjV4lz-TbRacSYw0Xr9u7dzuAGZErJ6NQ3eK35FTR1zTxp6JcFxrauQ8hQiP3E16UL-yt4NkeXYBJ2apYSSNwGh3bh-ZudbVXsJB2i2WA8uTLxJ-ZoWy6aaGZIm31gMXZvQLUwjfoYn_3t2Upldm3S-Lpm7Kmw2ezq9fYPaze1h2S2-ZVyqDOmDB-yTR8cnLfu6ZvDWch9RmI7QaufU9e9jXfQKEzfk3govz8CIMUkP83BFrYlmciHEMdDe-IMyvII7oZw5Sk7yNEpRpSk4EgbmN76KQE0E3ubcdgc3bQfd6mQv9FAiVsoI8I9h1l5dTiXFUxGRokHpmTPkvcqGMcKYQkbGEeLEdCdSMyyo8xPgF61cuV0Y3y3XJ-cUWBtRkce8voc5vKI9nl3rAGelGK2QYC1wt_IQ==\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"command\":\"python3 /home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/scripts/query_slm_expert_backup.py --help\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000}","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05ae207fdae919ce0169d800e928e4819197ef01663b717b2b\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Done.\n\nChanged `slm-expert-backup` so it now:\n- calls `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/chat`\n- sends only `{\"question\": \"...\"}` as the request body\n- ignores domains and any other extra payload fields\n\nI also updated the skill docs and reference template to match the new behavior. If you want, I can also make the main `slm-expert` skill behave the same way.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05ae207fdae919ce0169d800e94730819184d1493bdc187796\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage"